---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: lspkit — One engine. Every surface.
---
{# [WEB-DESIGN] Fieldwork: editorial hierarchy and an engineering plate. #}
<div class="home-shell">
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal" aria-hidden="true"></span> The language server toolkit</p>
      <h1 id="hero-title">One engine.<br><span>Every surface.</span></h1>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-aside">
      <p>Good tools start with solid foundations. Shared infrastructure for language servers, built to get out of your way.</p>
      <a class="text-link" href="/docs/">Explore the toolkit <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <figure class="engineering-plate">
    <img src="/assets/images/engine.svg" width="1440" height="600" alt="An orange engine connects through precise circuit paths to two dark terminal surfaces, representing LSP and MCP.">
    <figcaption><span>FIG. A — Shared foundations, connected surfaces.</span><span>LSP / MCP / RUST</span></figcaption>
  </figure>
  <section class="journal-preview" aria-labelledby="journal-heading">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="journal-heading">From the workbench.</h2><a class="text-link" href="/blog/">All notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
    {% for post in collections.posts | reverse %}
    <article class="journal-row">
      <span class="eyebrow">Field note / {{ loop.index }}</span>
      <div><h3><a href="{{ post.url }}">{{ post.data.title }} <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></h3><p>{{ post.data.excerpt }}</p></div>
      <time datetime="{{ post.date | isoDate }}">{{ post.date | dateFormat }}</time>
    </article>
    {% endfor %}
  </section>
</div>
